# Standalone starter — developed here, but never committed into this repo's
# history. It carries its own git repo and MIT license and is destined for a
# public repository of its own. Ignored (not just excluded) so `git add -A`
# cannot pull it in and `git clean -fd` cannot delete it.
examples/saas-starter/

# Local agent/tool settings. NOT tracked: these hold provider tokens in
# plaintext, and this one sits at the repo root where `git add -A` would sweep
# it into a commit — after which gitleaks scans history forever.
settings.local.json
**/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.local.json
